  "because": {
    "title": "The biggest mind-shift",
    "explain": "\"Es\" = always true. \"Está\" = right now.",
    "key": "Is this who they ARE, or how they HAPPEN TO BE? Always = es. Now = está.",
    "fun": "\"He is dead\" uses ESTÁ — death is something that happened!",
    "src": "Latin \"esse\" (to exist) plus \"sedēre\" (to sit) became \"ser\"; \"stare\" (to stand) became \"estar\". Sitting is settled, standing is passing through — the rule is baked into where the words came from. It takes you a long way, though not everywhere: an event's location uses ser — \"La fiesta es en mi casa.\""
  },
